    "explanation": "To both parties: the merits of this no-show point one way, but the case cannot be finished by the automated pipeline, so I am escalating it and holding the SGD 4.00 rather than collecting or refunding it. What the record shows (TRP-09108). All four conditions for a chargeable no-show under POL-NS-01 are met: (a) the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-08 09:30:20; (b) the GPS trace places the driver 24.01 m from the pickup pin — well inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius — from the first qualifying fix at 09:30:00, ahead of the arrival event; (c) the driver held position for a continuous 330 seconds (one run, 34 fixes, 0.0 kph), measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and so 30 seconds over the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum; and (d) no boarding is recorded and the driver terminated the trip at 09:35:30 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. Nothing displaces that. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) is not in play — the driver was inside the arrival radius, not between it and the 400 m ceiling. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: the chat log holds no locating or coordinating message from the rider (only the system arrival notice and the driver's 'Waiting at PLQ 3 pickup bay.'), and independently the rider's own track sits 519.4 m from the pin with 0 qualifying fixes, far outside the 150 m rider-presence radius. POL-NS-05 does not bite: at the arrival marker the driver was stationary at 0.0 kph, 24.01 m from the pin, and the clock skew between the first fix and the arrival event is 20 seconds, inside the 90-second POL-NS-08(a) tolerance. POL-NS-06 is not engaged because there is no shortfall to excuse — no accumulation across intervals is needed, so the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09108-01 (null payload, weight 0.0) is simply not relied on. The SGD 4.00 charged reconciles with the fee schedule: the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is SGD 4.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect for the rider to exploit. On those merits the charge would stand and the driver would be due 80% of the fee — SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00 (POL-NS-07). Why the case escalates. POL-NS-07's anti-farming check reads driver_profile and requires both limbs. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more), and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 70 is 0.10, above the 0.08 rate limb. Both limbs are met, so compensation is withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). This is the pattern the rider asked to have reviewed, and it sits on the driver's record: the rider's own counters fire nothing (rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles, so POL-NS-09(c) does not fire either). Escalation is terminal: the disputed SGD 4.00 is placed on hold, neither collected nor refunded, while a human reviewer looks at it, and POL-NS-07's direction to refund the rider in full is recorded in the packet. Confidence is 0.9; the deciding facts rest on the trip record, the GPS trace, the fare breakdown and the driver profile, none of which is below full weight, and the only zero-weight artifact (the missing advisory) is not relied on. The open question for the reviewer is whether the driver's 30-day no-show termination pattern is genuine fee-farming or ordinary high-volume work, to be settled with that refund direction in mind."
